<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Brzeg</h1><p class="st-meta">1311 CE – 1675 CE · capital Brzeg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Silesian Piast duchy on the Oder whose Lutheran dukes and Renaissance castle outlasted almost every other branch of the dynasty.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1311 the sons of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-the-fat">Henry V of Legnica</a> divided their inheritance, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-iii-the-generous">Bolesław III the Generous</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brzeg">Brzeg</a> (Brieg) on the Oder as his duchy, separating it from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-legnica">Duchy of Legnica</a>. In 1329 Bolesław did homage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-bohemia">King John of Bohemia</a>, placing Brzeg under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brzeg">Brzeg</a> was often held together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legnica">Legnica</a> under one duke, and its rulers were among the leading Silesian princes. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-legnica">Duke Frederick II</a> introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Lutheran Reformation</a> in the 1520s and in 1537 made an inheritance treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-ii-of-brieg">George II</a> the castle was rebuilt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> style, with a gatehouse adorned with statues of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piasts</a>, and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gymnasium">gymnasium</a> was founded in 1569.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-william-duke-of-legnica">George William</a>, the last Silesian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast</a>, died in 1675, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> as kings of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a> took the duchy, ignoring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg's</a> claim. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick II of Prussia</a> later used that claim to justify his invasion of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> won in 1742. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brzeg">Brzeg</a> became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-brzeg.jpg" alt="Duchy of Brzeg" width="320" height="298"><figcaption>Image: ŚląskiMaper · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_%C5%9Al%C4%85ska_z_ksi%C4%99stwami.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1311 CE – 1675 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brzeg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bolesław III the Generous, George II, George William</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Brieg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1493&amp;focus=duchy-of-brzeg" aria-label="Duchy of Brzeg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5077 413 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Brzeg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5397 669L5367 659M5397 669L5330 692"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5367 659h0M5330 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5397 669h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5397 669h0"/></svg></a><figcap